Nice Friday, for me. At first I had almost nothing, and I was a bit dejected seeing there were quite a few names and brands in the fill. In the end though I solved the puzzle without outside help, and in typical Friday time. I enjoyed the ambiguity and misdirection in many of the clues.

@SP
@Wyra
(And other gamers)

I have another video game recommendation. For the past week I've been playing the 2023 isometric cRPG "Warhammer 40,000: Rogue Trader" on my PS5 (it's available on PC, too; dunno about iOS). I'm loving it. To me it feels like a blend of two of my favorite game series of all time: Knights of the Old Republic and Mass Effect. The game blends isometric adventuring with space exploration and space combat. The turn-based combat system is really well executed. The story (so far) is very engaging. My main protagonist gets to make many tough and meaningful choices (progressing along three unique paths), which feels great. There are loads of interesting characters with stories and character arcs of their own. The writing is some of the best I've seen in a video game. The music creates an appropriate atmosphere. The graphics aren't amazing by 2026 standards but they're good enough to create the feel of a unique universe with diverse locations. Speaking of the universe: I have never experienced the world of Warhammer 40,000 before, and I'm finding getting to know it very interesting. The controls on the PS5 are a bit awkward but I'm managing. So far it's 10/10 for me.

